      "blocks": [
        { "type": "hero" },
        { "type": "problem_intro" },
        { "type": "problem_card", "settings": { "title": "Risk of Nail Splitting and Damage", "body": "Clippers crush before they cut. Even with a steady hand, that crushing force frequently splits the nail — and a split nail isn't just painful. It opens the nail bed to bacteria and debris, raising the risk of infection with every step your pet takes." } },
        { "type": "problem_card", "settings": { "title": "The Danger of Cutting the Quick", "body": "Inside every nail is the quick — a bundle of nerves and blood vessels. Clippers make it frighteningly easy to cut into it, causing sharp pain, bleeding, and swelling. And one bad cut is all it takes: your pet doesn't forget it, and the next trim starts harder than the last." } },
        { "type": "problem_card", "settings": { "title": "The Hidden Toll on Walking and Joints", "body": "Overgrown or badly trimmed nails push back into the paw with every step. Over time they change how your pet stands and walks, stressing joints and posture. Your pet can't tell you their paws hurt — they just live with it." } },
        { "type": "solution" },
        { "type": "mechanism" },
        { "type": "features_heading" },
        { "type": "feature", "settings": { "eyebrow": "01 — THE MOTOR", "title": "Ultra-Quiet Operation for Truly Relaxed Grooming", "body": "The CalmPaw Plus runs at under 40 dB — softer than a quiet conversation, and dramatically quieter than standard grinders. It's engineered to stay below the threshold that fires your pet's startle reflex, so there's no trigger left to fear — which is why so many pets simply settle in, and some doze off mid-trim." } },
        { "type": "feature", "settings": { "eyebrow": "02 — THE LIGHT", "title": "Built-In LED Light: See Exactly Where to Stop", "body": "The scariest part of nail care is the guessing — especially on dark or black nails where the quick is invisible. The CalmPaw Plus has the answer most grinders don't: a built-in LED light that illuminates the nail as you work, so you can watch your progress and stop well before the sensitive quick. No guessing games. Dark nails become as easy as light ones." } },
        { "type": "feature", "settings": { "eyebrow": "03 — THE HEAD", "title": "Diamond Smoothing Head: Gradual, Never Sudden", "body": "A stainless-steel body and a diamond smoothing head spinning at 7,500 RPM take the nail down in short, light passes — there is no sudden cut, and you control exactly how much comes off. Gentle enough for cats, rabbits, and small pets; for very large dogs with thick nails it still works — just go a little slower." } },
        { "type": "feature", "settings": { "eyebrow": "04 — THE GRIP", "title": "Comfortable Grip for Steady, Effortless Handling", "body": "Lightweight, balanced, and shaped to rest in your palm — right- or left-handed — so your free hand stays where it belongs: reassuring your pet. A steady hold means precise control, shorter sessions, and a calmer trim for everyone." } },
        { "type": "feature", "settings": { "eyebrow": "05 — THE BATTERY", "title": "USB-C Rechargeable, Ready Whenever They Are", "body": "Charge with the included USB-C cable — a full charge takes about 3 hours and gives you up to 2 hours of trimming, enough for several pets across many sessions. Since a calm trim takes about a minute, one charge lasts most homes for weeks. Tip: charge it fully before first use." } },
        { "type": "compare" },
        { "type": "proof" },
        { "type": "guarantee" },
        { "type": "faq_heading" },
        { "type": "faq_item" },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "Is it safe for all pet sizes and breeds?", "answer": "<p>Yes. It works on dogs, cats, rabbits, guinea pigs, and other small pets. It shines on small and medium pets; for very large dogs with thick nails it still works — just go a little slower and take short, light passes.</p>" } },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "How much should I trim at a time?", "answer": "<p>Just a little. Smooth the nail in short, light passes instead of one big grind. Take off a small amount, check, and stop before you reach the soft pink part (the quick). On dark nails, turn on the LED light and watch the lit cut surface — when the center changes texture or color, that's your signal to stop.</p>" } },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "How does it help prevent over-trimming?", "answer": "<p>Because it sands gradually, you control exactly how much comes off — there is no sudden cut like clippers. You approach the quick in tiny, visible steps, and the built-in LED light helps you see the nail clearly so you simply stop before you reach it.</p>" } },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "What if my pet is still nervous at first?", "answer": "<p>Totally normal — especially for pets with a rough nail-day history. Their fear was learned, which means it can be unlearned. Let them sniff it while it's off, then run it nearby so the quiet hum becomes background noise. Pair it with treats, do one or two nails at a time, and build up over a few short sessions. The full step-by-step plan is in your free Calm-Trim Guide.</p>" } },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "How long does the battery last?", "answer": "<p>Up to about 2 hours of trimming on a full charge — plenty for several pets across multiple sessions. Since a calm weekly trim takes about a minute, one charge lasts most homes for weeks.</p>" } },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "How do I charge it, and how long does it take?", "answer": "<p>Charge it with the included USB-C cable from any standard USB charger or computer port. A full charge takes about 3 hours. Tip: charge it fully before the first use.</p>" } },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "Can I use it on cats, rabbits, guinea pigs, or other small pets?", "answer": "<p>Yes. The quiet, low-vibration design is gentle enough for cats, rabbits, guinea pigs, and other small animals — not just dogs. One CalmPaw Plus covers the whole household.</p>" } },
        { "type": "faq_item", "settings": { "question": "Why can't I just walk my dog to keep their nails short?", "answer": "<p>Walking helps a little on hard surfaces, but most dogs still grow nails faster than they wear them down — especially the dewclaws, which never touch the ground. And walks do nothing for cats. A one-minute weekly smoothing keeps every nail at a healthy length — evenly, safely, on your schedule.</p>" } },
